# This repository's root is the home directory, C:\Users\David, because the
# first `git init` ran there rather than in the project folder. The project is
# securejobva/, and every tracked file is under it apart from the 32-byte
# README GitHub made with the repo, this file, and the two npm files below.
#
# So: ignore everything at the root, then name back what belongs to the
# project. Without this, `git status` lists the whole home directory —
# NTUSER.DAT, AppData, Downloads, the browser profiles, the other projects —
# exits non-zero on the Windows junctions it cannot read, and `git add -A`
# from anywhere would stage all of it for two public remotes.
#
# package.json and package-lock.json are here rather than in securejobva/
# because Vercel's Root Directory is securejobva/, and a package.json in there
# would add an npm install to a build vercel.json defines as `node build.mjs`
# with no dependencies. They pin the one dev dependency that
# securejobva/tools/check-cleanup.mjs needs; tracked, because otherwise a
# fresh clone has no record that it needs libpg-query at all, and that tool is
# the only thing that has ever read the removal block in
# sql/cleanup-paying-half.sql. node_modules/ stays ignored by the /* above.
#
# securejobva/.gitignore still does its own work inside the project; this file
# only decides what git looks at in the first place.
/*

!/securejobva/
!/README.md
!/.gitignore
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
